    given-names: Wensen
    alias: Cveinnt
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-01"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Cveinnt/kepler"
url: "https://kepler-harness.vercel.app"
abstract: >-
  Kepler is an open-source agent harness that reaches a server-verified exact
  100.00 RHAE on all 25 public ARC-AGI-3 games with one frozen Claude Opus 5
  configuration and no score-conditioned reruns. On that board, 181 of 183
  completed levels use no more actions than the median-human baseline. The
  retained board runs use 8,256 environment actions, with 7,292 in the original
  local scored-level results and 7,202 on the public replay card. Complete
  campaign action accounting is
  still pending. The provider record costs $777.72 at current API
  list-equivalent rates. The release includes complete
  provider-record resource accounting, score-lineage tools, an enforced
  zero-game-priors check, negative results, and incident reports for two
  integrity failures caught in our own experiments. A public companion dataset
  provides 50 final-board run ledgers, human baselines, captured CLI output,
  and standalone verification programs. Earlier development
  stages and incidents remain documented separately in the repository.
identifiers:
